---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Disclaimer — Army Pink" description="What Army Pink's website, services, and content are — and aren't. Information on professional advice, wellness content, crisis use, and limitation of liability.">

  <div class="legal-layout container">

    <!-- LEFT: STICKY SIDEBAR -->
    <aside class="legal-sidebar" aria-label="Disclaimer sections">
      <nav class="legal-nav">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#no-professional-advice" data-section-link>No professional advice</a></li>
          <li><a href="#wellness-content" data-section-link>Wellness content</a></li>
          <li><a href="#crisis-use" data-section-link>Not a crisis service</a></li>
          <li><a href="#third-party-services" data-section-link>Third-party services</a></li>
          <li><a href="#no-guarantees" data-section-link>No guarantees</a></li>
          <li><a href="#limitation" data-section-link>Limitation of liability</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes" data-section-link>Changes to this disclaimer</a></li>
          <li><a href="#contact" data-section-link>Contact us</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
    </aside>

    <!-- RIGHT: CONTENT -->
    <article class="legal-content">

      <header class="legal-header">
        <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: May 22, 2026</p>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          Army Pink is a survivor-led nonprofit. We do our best to help, but we want to
          be clear about what our website, content, and services are — and what they
          aren't. Please read this page alongside our
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a> and
          <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms of Service</a>.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- §1 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="no-professional-advice">
        <h2>1. No professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          Information provided on armypink.org, in our Discord community, in SMS
          messages, or through any Army Pink program is for general informational and
          educational purposes only. It is <strong>not a substitute</strong> for
          professional medical, mental health, legal, financial, or other expert advice.
        </p>
        <p>
          Always seek the advice of a qualified professional — a doctor, licensed
          therapist, attorney, or domestic violence advocate — for questions about your
          specific situation. Never disregard professional advice or delay seeking it
          because of something you read or heard through Army Pink.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §2 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="wellness-content">
        <h2>2. Wellness content</h2>
        <p>
          Yoga, meditation, breathwork, and other wellness content offered through Army
          Pink — including content from partners such as Do Yoga With Me — is intended
          as a supportive practice, not as medical treatment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before beginning any wellness practice, consult your healthcare provider,
          especially if you:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Have a medical condition or recent injury</li>
          <li>Are pregnant or recently postpartum</li>
          <li>Have a history of trauma-related dissociation, panic, or seizures</li>
          <li>Are taking medications that affect heart rate, blood pressure, or balance</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If a practice causes pain, distress, or a flashback, stop and seek support.
          Trauma-informed care matters — go at your own pace.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §3 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="crisis-use">
        <h2>3. Not a crisis service</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Army Pink is not a 24/7 crisis line.</strong> Our website, contact
          form, Discord community, and SMS program are not monitored continuously, and
          we cannot guarantee an immediate response.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are in immediate danger or experiencing a crisis, please contact a
          service designed for that purpose:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Emergency:</strong> Call <a href="tel:911">911</a></li>
          <li><strong>National Domestic Violence Hotline:</strong>
          <a href="tel:18007997233">1-800-799-7233</a> (24/7)</li>
          <li><strong>Crisis Text Line:</strong> Text <strong>START</strong> to
          <strong>88788</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Live chat:</strong>
          <a href="https://www.thehotline.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">thehotline.org</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- §4 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="third-party-services">
        <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Army Pink works with and links to third-party services we trust, including
          (but not limited to) Do Yoga With Me, Discord, Twilio, Givebutter, Mailchimp,
          and The National DV Hotline. These services have their own terms of service
          and privacy policies, which we encourage you to review.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not control these services and are not responsible for their content,
          availability, security, or practices. If you experience an issue with a
          third-party service, please reach out to that service directly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §5 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="no-guarantees">
        <h2>5. No guarantees</h2>
        <p>
          We make reasonable efforts to keep information on this site accurate,
          up-to-date, and safe — but we cannot guarantee:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The accuracy or completeness of any information at any given time</li>
          <li>The availability of the site, Discord community, or SMS program</li>
          <li>The outcome or impact of any program, ride, workshop, or resource</li>
          <li>The safety or behavior of any third-party service or partner</li>
          <li>That any specific result will follow from following our guidance</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Survivor situations are deeply individual, and what helps one person may not
          help another. Always trust your own judgment and consult qualified
          professionals where appropriate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §6 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="limitation">
        <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, Army Pink and its founders, staff,
          volunteers, contributors, contractors, and partners shall not be liable for
          any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, special, or punitive damages
          arising out of or related to your use of armypink.org, the Discord community,
          the SMS program, or any other Army Pink program or service.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using our site or services, you agree that your use is at your own
          discretion and risk. Nothing in this disclaimer is intended to exclude
          liability that cannot be excluded under applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §7 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="changes">
        <h2>7. Changes to this disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this disclaimer from time to time. When we make material
          changes, we will update the "last updated" date at the top of this page.
          Continued use of the site or our services after changes constitutes
          acceptance of the revised disclaimer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- §8 -->
      <section class="privacy-section" id="contact">
        <h2>8. Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions about this disclaimer:</p>
        <address class="privacy-contact">
          <strong>Army Pink</strong><br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:support@armypink.org">support@armypink.org</a><br>
          Phone: <a href="tel:12135795051">(213) 579-5051</a>
        </address>
      </section>

    </article>
  </div>

  <!-- Sticky sidebar active-section highlight -->
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var links = document.querySelectorAll('[data-section-link]');
      if (!links.length) return;
      var sections = Array.from(links).map(function (a) {
        return document.querySelector(a.getAttribute('href'));
      }).filter(Boolean);

      function setActive(id) {
        links.forEach(function (a) {
          a.classList.toggle('is-active', a.getAttribute('href') === '#' + id);
        });
      }

      var observer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
        var visible = entries
          .filter(function (e) { return e.isIntersecting; })
          .sort(function (a, b) { return a.boundingClientRect.top - b.boundingClientRect.top; });
        if (visible[0]) setActive(visible[0].target.id);
      }, {
        rootMargin: '-100px 0px -60% 0px',
        threshold: 0
      });

      sections.forEach(function (s) { observer.observe(s); });
      if (sections[0]) setActive(sections[0].id);
    })();
  </script>

</Layout>
